      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-222480",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following statement:\n\n> Given that $A$ and $B$ are sets, $A\u222aB^(\u2015)\u2286A^(\u2015)\u2229B^(\u2015)$.\n\nA proof of this statement is given below.\n\n> $L1$: Suppose $x \u2208 A\u222aB^(\u2015)$.\n> $L2$: So, $x \u2209 A\u222aB$.\n> $L3$: The former is equivalent to $\u00ac(x \u2208 A\u222aB)$.\n> $L4$: Then, $\u00ac(x \u2208 A\u2228x \u2208 B)$.\n> $L5$: Then, $\u00ac(x \u2208 A)\u2227\u00ac(x \u2208 B)$.\n> $L6$: As a result, $x \u2209 A\u2227x \u2209 B$.\n> $L7$: Thus, $x \u2208 A^(\u2015)$ and $x \u2208 B^(\u2015)$.\n> $L8$: Hence, $x \u2208 A^(\u2015)\u2229B^(\u2015)$.\n> $L9$: Therefore, $A\u222aB^(\u2015)\u2286A^(\u2015)\u2229B^(\u2015)$.\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nLine $L2$ follows from line $L1$ by the definition of {{field-1}}\n\nLine $L5$ follows from line $L4$ by\n{{field-2}} {{field-3}}\n\nLine $L9$ follows from lines\n{{field-4}}\nand $L8$ by\n{{field-5}} {{field-6}}"
    }
  ],
